Included Files:

List.c:        	  Source code for the List ADT.
Matrix.c:         Source code for the Matrix ADT.
Sparse.c:         Source code for the Sparse program. Contains Main.
MatrixTest.c:     Source code for the test program for the Matrix ADT.
ListTest.c:       Source code for the test program for the List ADT.

List.h:       Include .h file for the necessary List ADT functions.
Matrix.h:     Include .h file for the necessary Matrix ADT functions.
makefile:     Makefile for included executables. Usage instructions inside.
README:       Usage and instructions for the program.

USAGE:

Run "make" to create Spare executable.
Run by using the command:
	Sparse <infile> <outfile>
The Sparse program accepts Matrix vertices via the infile, calculates various
martix operarions on the Matrices, and prints the results to the out

Notes about the assignment:
	At the time of writing, I have yet to solve a major floating point
    conversion error. In all likelyhood, I will submit an assignment in which the tests are off by ~.1 per measurement.

Other make commands:
	make clean: removes generated files
	make MatrixTest: makes the MatrixTest executable
		run with: ./MatrixTest
	make ListTest: makes the ListTest executable
                run with: ./ListTest
	make check: runs valgrind on Sparse, testing for memory leaks.
		    requires files "infile" and "outfile" for testing.
